---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Corrections Policy | Plain Act"
  description="How Plain Act receives, reviews, and updates material corrections to published management content."
  path="/corrections-policy/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home', url:'/'}, {name:'Corrections Policy', url:'/corrections-policy/'}]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Corrections policy</p>
      <h1>Errors should be easy to report and clear to fix.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Plain Act reviews reported factual errors, broken references, misleading wording, and material omissions. This policy describes the correction path without promising real-time response or review.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-2 section-sm">
        <article class="card flat">
          <h2>How to report a correction</h2>
          <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Include the page URL, the specific statement or section, what you believe is wrong, and—when available—the source or evidence supporting the correction.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card flat">
          <h2>What qualifies</h2>
          <p>Examples include incorrect facts, outdated platform information, broken or misrepresented sources, wrong product metadata, materially unclear wording, or a statement that creates a misleading impression.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card flat">
          <h2>How material corrections are handled</h2>
          <p>When a reported issue is confirmed, the affected page may be corrected, clarified, expanded, or removed. Related internal links or metadata may also be updated when the error affects them.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card flat">
          <h2>Dates and review notes</h2>
          <p>A page should not display a fabricated review date. If an actual material review or correction occurs and a date is shown, it should reflect that real event.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="notice">
        <strong>No real-time guarantee.</strong>
        <p>Plain Act does not promise immediate correction or continuous monitoring of every page. Reports are reviewed as publishing capacity allows, with priority given to material factual or user-impacting issues.</p>
        <p><a href="/editorial-policy/">Read the Editorial Policy</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
